## Building a “Private Messaging” Feature in a Bolt‑Supabase App  
*(No prior coding experience required – I’ll walk you through every step in plain language and include ready‑to‑copy snippets you can paste into your project.)*

---

## 1. What we’ll build

- **Users can send a single text message to another user.**  
- The message appears in the **conversation view** of both participants.  
- Messages are **private** – only the sender and receiver can see them.  
- Messages are stored **real‑time** in Supabase’s PostgreSQL database and instantly shown to the receiver using Supabase’s Realtime feature.

---

## 2. Pre‑requisites

| Item | How to get it | Why needed |
|------|---------------|------------|
| **Bolt** project | Created on <https://start.bolt.com> | Front‑end UI framework (React + Chakra UI). |
| **Supabase** project | <https://supabase.com> (free tier) | Backend database, auth, and realtime. |
| **Bolt CLI** | `npm i -g @bolt-build/cli` | For running/packaging the app locally. |

> **Tip:** If you already have a Bolt project, just add a few files – no new folders needed.

---

## 3. Step‑by‑step build

### 3.1 Add Supabase configuration to your Bolt project

1. In your Bolt project root, create a file called `supabase.js` (or `supabase.ts` if you prefer TypeScript):

```js
// supabase.js
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';

const supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL;
const supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY;

export const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey);
```

2. Add the environment variables to your `.env` file:

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your-supabase-url-from-dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key
```

(You can find these values in the Supabase dashboard → *Project Settings → API*.)

---

### 3.2 Create the **messages** table in Supabase

1. Open the Supabase dashboard.  
2. Go → **Table Editor** → **New Table**.  

| Field | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|-------|------|-------------|-------|
| id | `bigint` | `auto increment` | Primary key |
| sender_id | `uuid` | `not null`, reference to `auth.users` | Which user sent the message |
| receiver_id | `uuid` | `not null`, reference to `auth.users` | Which user received the message |
| body | `text` | `not null` | The message text |
| inserted_at | `timestamp with time zone` | default `now()` | When the message was created |

3. Click **Save**.  
4. Create a row‑level security policy so that only the **sender or receiver** can see the row:

```
SELECT
  id,
  sender_id,
  receiver_id,
  body,
  inserted_at
FROM
  public.messages
WHERE
  (sender_id = auth.uid() OR receiver_id = auth.uid());
```

> You can enable Realtime on the table by clicking the **Realtime** toggle next to the table in the dashboard.

---

### 3.3 Create the “Chat” component

Create a new component file: `components/Chat.js`

```jsx
// components/Chat.js
import { useEffect, useState, useRef } from "react";
import { supabase } from "../supabase";
import { Box, Input, Button, VStack, Text } from "@chakra-ui/react";

export default function Chat({ currentUser, friendId }) {
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([]);
  const [input, setInput] = useState("");
  const messagesEndRef = useRef(null);

  // 1️⃣ Load initial messages with friend
  useEffect(() => {
    const load = async () => {
      const { data, error } = await supabase
        .from("messages")
        .select("*")
        .or(`sender_id.eq.${friendId},receiver_id.eq.${friendId}`)
        .eq("sender_id", currentUser.id)
        .or(`receiver_id.eq.${currentUser.id},sender_id.eq.${currentUser.id}`);
      if (error) return alert(error);
      setMessages(data);
    };
    load();
  }, [friendId, currentUser.id]);

  // 2️⃣ Realtime subscription for new messages
  useEffect(() => {
    const subscription = supabase
      .channel("public:messages")
      .on(
        "postgres_changes",
        { event: "*", schema: "public", table: "messages" },
        (payload) => {
          const { new: msg } = payload;
          // Only keep messages that involve this chat
          if (
            (msg.sender_id === currentUser.id &&
              msg.receiver_id === friendId) ||
            (msg.receiver_id === currentUser.id &&
              msg.sender_id === friendId)
          ) {
            setMessages((prev) => [...prev, msg]);
          }
        }
      )
      .subscribe();

    return () => supabase.removeChannel(subscription);
  }, [friendId, currentUser.id]);

  // 3️⃣ Send a new message
  const sendMessage = async () => {
    if (!input.trim()) return;
    const { data, error } = await supabase
      .from("messages")
      .insert([
        {
          sender_id: currentUser.id,
          receiver_id: friendId,
          body: input.trim(),
        },
      ])
      .single();
    if (error) return alert(error);
    setInput("");
  };

  // 4️⃣ Scroll to bottom when messages update
  useEffect(() => {
    messagesEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth" });
  }, [messages]);

  return (
    <VStack
      w="100%"
      h="80vh"
      border="1px solid"
      borderColor="gray.200"
      borderRadius="md"
      p={4}
      overflowY="auto"
    >
      {messages.map((msg) => (
        <Box
          key={msg.id}
          alignSelf={msg.sender_id === currentUser.id ? "flex-end" : "flex-start"}
          bg={msg.sender_id === currentUser.id ? "blue.100" : "gray.100"}
          p={2}
          borderRadius="md"
          maxW="80%"
        >
          <Text>{msg.body}</Text>
